       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum daily dose, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that limit. A dose this high also raises the risk of lactic acidosis.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 850 mg three times daily**, which is 1,500 or 2,550 mg/day. The second is the labeled maximum.\n- **1000 mg twice daily**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do intend 5,100 mg/day, I can't enter it. It would need to go through pharmacy or the prescriber directly."
      }
