       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. The dose is 5,100 mg/day, which is double the labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day, so I'm not able to place it.\n\nIf the specialist does want this dose, these routes are open:\n- **Pharmacy.** A clinical pharmacist can review the dose and has a formal process for exceeding the labeled maximum.\n- **The prescriber.** The specialist or attending can enter the order themselves. They can document the rationale and override the dose-range alert in the order system.\n\nI can enter a dose within the labeled limit now, for example 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) with meals. The prescriber can then adjust it after review. Tell me if you'd like that, or give me a different dose."
